  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Plugin Star Radar · dsh-plugin-star-radar",
      "text": "A \"what should I install?\" reference for people new to DeepSeek Harness (DSH).\n\nIt answers one question: **which DSH plugins are people actually paying attention to and installing?**"
    },
    {
      "section": "Plugin Star Radar · dsh-plugin-star-radar",
      "text": "- Ranked by **GitHub stars**;\n- Every card also shows **npm downloads over the last 30 days**, and you can re-sort by that;\n- **3000+ stars OR 100k+ downloads in 30 days** gets a plugin **listed**;\n- Once listed, a plugin **stays listed** even after it falls below both thresholds: it moves to a labelled `已跌出 · 保留` group for `retainDays` (180 by default) with its last measured numbers, so it is still findable months later."
    },
    {
      "section": "Why two metrics",
      "text": "| Downloads only | Stars only | Both |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Older plugins get pushed out by newer download spikes and become hard to find | A brand-new plugin that is installed in bulk but not starred yet is missed | What people keep watching *and* what gets installed right now |\n\nInclusion is the **union**; ranking is stars-first. A plugin that cools down stays on the page, which is exactly what a reference list needs."
    },
    {
      "section": "Desktop (recommended)",
      "text": "Settings → Plugins → Install, then paste:\n\n```\ndsh-plugin-star-radar\n```\n\nOr press the **安装 / Install** button on any card in this plugin."
    },
    {
      "section": "CLI",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-plugin-star-radar\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Local checkout",
      "text": "```bash\npnpm add \"file:D:/path/to/dsh-plugin-star-radar\"\n```\n\nAdd `\"dsh-plugin-star-radar\"` to `dsh.profile.bundles` in the profile's `package.json`, then restart DSH.\n\n> Migrating from the older `dsh-plugin-radar` / `dsh-plugin-download-radar`? Disable and remove the old one first — all three register the same section id (`plugin-radar`), so only one may be enabled."
    },
    {
      "section": "What the page does",
      "text": "- **Groups** by star band (★ 5k+ / ★ 3k+ / download-only) so the tiers are obvious at a glance;\n- **Search** across name, package, description and category;\n- **Category filter** from the market index;\n- **Sort** by stars / 30-day downloads / name;\n- **Details** per card: stars, downloads, why it is listed, listing date, Node/DSH ranges, OS/CPU, package size, permission notes, manual install command, repo links;\n- **One-click install** through the official `pluginManager.installBundle`, falling back to the profile's pnpm with a copyable manual command."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "In the profile's `cordis.patch.yml`:\n\n```yaml\n- id: plugin-radar\n  config:\n    minStars: 3000\n    minDownloads: 100000"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "| Key | Default | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `minStars` | `3000` | star count that gets a plugin listed |\n| `minDownloads` | `100000` | 30-day download count that gets a plugin listed |\n| `retainDays` | `180` | days a plugin stays visible after falling below both thresholds |\n| `intervalHours` | `6` | background refresh interval (1–168) |\n| `catalogTtlHours` | `12` | market index cache |\n| `metaTtlHours` | `24` | npm manifest cache |\n| `maxManifest` | `80` | how many manifests feed the environment notes |\n| `manifestBudgetMs` | `90000` | manifest phase budget; overruns are skipped, never block the board |\n| `catalogUrl` / `npmRegistry` | official | point them at a mirror if needed |\n| `dataDir` | `<profile>/.dsh-plugin-radar` | cache directory |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Where the data comes from",
      "text": "| Data | Source |\n| --- | --- |\n| plugin list, GitHub stars, 30-day downloads, category, description, icon | `https://awesome-dsh-plugin.com/plugins.json` — **one** request for everything |\n| Node/DSH ranges, `os`/`cpu`, install scripts, package size | `https://registry.npmjs.org/<pkg>/latest`, only for listed plugins |\n\nTwo deliberate choices:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Where the data comes from",
      "text": "1. **No per-package npm downloads history calls.** `api.npmjs.org/downloads/range` answers HTTP 429 under bursts, which is what made an earlier version of this plugin stall mid-refresh. One catalog request cannot rate-limit itself.\n2. **Manifest reads are optional and budgeted.** Missing notes never block the board."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```bash\nnode scripts/build-client.mjs      # client.css + client.src.js -> client.js\nnode --test \"test/*.test.mjs\"      # offline unit tests\nnode scripts/live-check.mjs        # real market index, prints the board"
    },
    {
      "section": "Publishing",
      "text": "There is no official DSH marketplace; community indexes fill the gap. See [docs/publishing.md](./docs/publishing.md)."
    },
    {
